From 773f15e978564f01f79db8ac2245dbbb5bf88066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:27:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_servers: zeo-terminals -- the terminals you share,
 readable by the agent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next §6.71. ACP's `terminal/*` reaches only terminals the agent
created, and Claude Agent (Plus) creates none, so the agent never saw
what runs beside it -- a dev server's errors, a test run, a build.

- A terminal is shared per tab, by the operator: `terminal::
  ToggleShareWithAgent`, in the terminal's context menu as "Share with
  Agent" / "Stop Sharing with Agent". A shared tab shows the agent's
  icon. Nothing is shared until the operator shares it.
- `zeo-terminals` is one more MCP server over MCP-over-ACP, declared
  beside `zeo-lsp` to an agent that advertised `mcpCapabilities.acp`,
  under `agent.zeo_terminals` (default on). Two read-only tools:
  `list_terminals` (id, title, folder, and whether a task runs or how it
  ended) and `read_terminal(id, lines)` -- the last non-empty lines,
  200 by default, at most 2000 and 256 KB, newest kept. It never writes
  to a terminal.
- A read is logged with the terminal and the sizes, never the content.
- Remote projects get no declaration: their terminals run on the
  remote host. A jail reaches it only when chosen in its Capabilities,
  like any proxied server (0215 lists it there).
- `Project::local_terminals` exposes the live local terminals the
  server filters.

The manual direction -- sending a terminal's lines to the agent -- is
Zed's existing "Add to Agent Thread" on a selection.

Tests: zeo_terminals.rs (the byte bound keeps the newest lines; the
tools are read-only); the MCP-over-ACP harness turns the server off
like zeo-lsp.
---

